## Sources and version notes

LangChain APIs and recommended architecture continue to evolve. This lesson follows the current official Python documentation while authoring and avoids older imports such as `LLMChain`, `ConversationBufferMemory`, and `RetrievalQA` that appeared in the previous page.

- [LangChain overview and `create_agent`](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/overview)
- [Models and the standard model interface](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/models)
- [Agents, tools, state, and structured output](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/agents)
- [Tool runtime context](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/tools)
- [Middleware and the agent loop](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/middleware/overview)
- [Prebuilt middleware controls](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/middleware/built-in)
- [Short-term memory and production checkpointers](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/short-term-memory)
